    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Broken Password Generator\r\n\r\n**Goal:** Use the loop debugging checklist to find and fix the bug so the generated password has the same number of characters as the number you enter.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**1. Run the app.**\r\n\r\n* Type a number and click **Generate Password**.\r\n* Look at the bottom of the app to compare the *expected* length and *actual* length.\r\n\r\n**2. Find the loop.**\r\n\r\nThis code was generated by AI from this prompt:\r\n\r\n> “Write a loop that builds a password with the number of characters the user enters.”\r\n\r\nBefore you change the code, use the **Loop Debugging Checklist** in your Unit Guide to test the loop.\r\n\r\n**3. Use the checklist.**\r\n* Does the loop start where expected?\r\n* Does it stop at the correct final value?\r\n* Does it run one extra time or stop too early?\r\n* Does the output match the requested behavior?\r\n\r\nMark any checklist item that reveals the bug.\r\n\r\n**4. Fix and test.**\r\n\r\n* Change the for-loop so it runs the correct number of times. Then test the app again with several different numbers. The expected and actual lengths should match each time.\r\n",
